  "summary": "I found four institutional-context issues. The NVDB claim that it lacks opening dates is overgeneralised from one linked record, and the paper omits the Statens vegvesen rule that registration happens early. Table 2 gives Grettefoss Bridge the status \"Planned\" although its own footnote says it opened on 3 November. The FINN.no county breakdown does not say how pre-2024 listings map to the post-2024 counties. The text says only Q1 2024 is missing, but the data gap runs from January to April 2024. External checks confirmed that Gemini 3.8 Flash, its September 2026 model card, the Google Cloud $300 trial credit and the Norwegian county boundaries are as described, so I raise no issue on those.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "INST-001",
      "category": "regulatory_context_incomplete",
      "finding_summary": "The paper says NVDB lacks opening dates and only records geometry registration, but it omits that Statens vegvesen requires registration early (at project design or construction start, well before opening). Registration dates therefore carry no stable lag to the opening date, and one record cannot show the one-month gap generalises.",
      "issue_type": "manuscript_issue",
      "severity": "medium",
      "confidence": "medium",
      "location": {
        "page": 8,
        "page_label": "8",
        "section": "4.3 Linking newspaper articles to administrative data",
        "text_quote": "NVDB does not record when a road opens to traffic,",
        "precision": "exact"
      },
      "claim_text": "NVDB does not record when a road opens to traffic, only when its geometry was registered; the newspaper articles therefore add an exact opening date that NVDB lacks.",
      "assessment": "partially",
      "cannot_verify_reason": null,
      "evidence_summary": "The manuscript bases this on one Homborsund record, whose geometry was registered 4 September 2026, one month before opening (Table 5). The conclusion and abstract present it as a general complementarity. Statens vegvesen's data-delivery page says data must be delivered early and well before opening, with new projects registered when the design phase starts and at the latest at construction start. So the NVDB registration date is a project-stage registration date whose lag to opening varies by project, and could be far longer than one month. The paper does not say which NVDB field or date it calls 'geometry registered' (for example start date of the road link). It does not explain the registration rules that make that date an unreliable proxy for opening. Section 8 does propose a systematic comparison with registration dates, which partly acknowledges the limit. I could not retrieve an authoritative NVDB statement on whether any separate opening-date or status attribute exists, so I do not claim NVDB has one.",
      "source_objects": [
        {
          "id": "M1",
          "type": "text",
          "label": "Page 8 text, Section 4.3",
          "path": "work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_008.md",
