      "claim_text": "Table 2 reports the Grettefoss Bridge project, with opening date 3 Nov 2026, as status 'Planned'.",
      "assessment": "no",
      "cannot_verify_reason": null,
      "evidence_summary": "The Table 2 row for Grettefoss Bridge gives status 'Planned', but footnote c says the opening was 'Confirmed to have opened 3 November as planned.' The Tromsø footnote is dated '6 November' and the paper is dated 9 November 2026, so the opening is in the past. The pilot rules in Section 3.1.4 require checking whether a planned date has passed. The Figure 1 caption and Section 3.1.4 treat both Tromsø and Grettefoss as planned openings and count only 2 openings that took place. Those counts can be read as at pilot extraction (2 September to 10 October). The table mixes the article-time and later status without labelling the as-of date. This affects interpretation of 'planned' versus 'actual' openings, a distinction the paper says matters for the coding rules. I cannot independently verify the real-world opening dates of these projects.",
